WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.160
Get the jab or get a new job. That's the&nbsp;
message from the government in Zimbabwe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:13.200
It's introducing a vaccination mandate for all of&nbsp;
its nearly 300,000 public sector workers. The idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.520
is to force those reluctant to get the&nbsp;
jab to finally roll up their sleeves.&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.320
Across Africa, there are still not enough people&nbsp;
getting vaccinated. Only about five percent of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:30.640
African population has so far been double jabbed.&nbsp;
That's compared to around 55 percent in Asia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.640
75 percent in Europe and 65&nbsp;
percent in South America.&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:44.160
A lack of vaccine is slowing the rollout across&nbsp;
Africa. But vaccine hesitancy is also posing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.000
growing challenge. Other African countries are&nbsp;
also considering making vaccination mandatory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.560
for their public sector workers.
Are mandates like this the best way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:02.400
to stamp out vaccine hesitancy? Privilege&nbsp;
Musvanhiri sent this report from Harare.&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:11.760
Garikai Mahlengwe is a teacher at a public&nbsp;
school in the capital Harare. He like many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.120
other civil servants was vaccinated, but&nbsp;
only out of the fear of losing his job.&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.800
Garikai considers mandatory&nbsp;
vaccination for public workers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.840
as discriminatory and a violation&nbsp;
of the freedom of choice.&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:33.920
"I feel we have been robbed of our rights&nbsp;
by the pandemic. This mandatory vaccination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.160
if it was mandatory to everyone, should&nbsp;
not have selected civil servants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:47.120
It seems as if civil servants are the&nbsp;
only human beings here and are the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.080
only spearheaders of COVID&nbsp;
19, which is totally wrong."&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.520
Despite the call for public workers&nbsp;
to be vaccinated, the vaccination rate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.560
has not gone up as expected.
There are hardly long queues at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.240
vaccination centers if compared to a few months&nbsp;
back when the country was hit by the third wave.&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:18.080
While vaccines maybe readily available at&nbsp;
vaccination centers like this one. It is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:26.160
the citizens’ response that is a bit low. It is&nbsp;
a trickle against what health authorities may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.400
anticipating. Perhaps because of the&nbsp;
conspiracy theories surrounding vaccines.&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:40.480
Zimbabwe is targeting vaccinating 60+ per&nbsp;
cent of its population, hoping to get close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:46.240
to herd immunity. That accounts for 10&nbsp;
million out of its 15 million citizens.&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.800
The government says mandatory&nbsp;
vaccination means just that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:58.080
Some individual rights have to be restricted.
The government is saying you need to be vaccinated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:05.440
to protect yourself and those that you serve.&nbsp;
Public servants are always working in public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:11.360
spaces and interacting with the public. We need to&nbsp;
make sure that all public servants are vaccinated.&nbsp;

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.120
Worker unions have challenged mandatory&nbsp;
vaccination in courts but are encouraging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.160
the government to provide vaccines to&nbsp;
all citizens willing to take up the jabs.&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:30.160
"It is illogical to force an employee&nbsp;
to get vaccinated at the same time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:36.240
allow the same employee to interact and&nbsp;
mingle with a person who is not vaccinated."&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:42.000
For Garikai Mahlengwe, a vaccination&nbsp;
card is now the passport to work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:49.040
At least he is guaranteed a salary.
However, his case is not unique - many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:59.840
countries across the world are now moving&nbsp;
towards COVID passports to access services.

